    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.2",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "354. Augustin born at Tagaste, Nov. 13; his parents, Patricius and Monnica; shortly afterwards enrolled among the Catechumens.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.3",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "370. Returns home from studying Rhetoric at Madaura, after an idle childhood, and from idleness falls into dissipation and sin.",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.4",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "371. Patricius dies; Augustin supported at Carthage by his mother, and his friend Romanianus; forms an illicit connection.",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.5",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "372. Birth of his son Adeodatus.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.6",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "373. Cicero’s Hortensius awakens in him a strong desire for true wisdom.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.7",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "374. He falls into the Manichæan heresy, and seduces several of his acquaintances into it. His mother’s earnest prayers for him; she is assured of his recovery.",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.8",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "376. Teaches Grammar at Tagaste; but soon returns to Carthage to teach Rhetoric—gains a prize.",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.9",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "379. Is recovered from study of Astrology—writes his books De pulchro et apto.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.10",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "382. Discovers the Manichæans to be in error, but falls into scepticism. Goes to Rome to teach Rhetoric.",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.11",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "385. Removes to Milan; his errors gradually removed through the teaching of Ambrose, but he is held back by the flesh; becomes again a Catechumen.",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.12",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "386. Studies St. Paul; converted through a voice from heaven; gives up his profession; writes against the Academics; prepares for Baptism.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.13",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.13",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "387. Is baptized by Bishop Ambrose, with his son Adeodatus. Death of his mother, Monnica, in her fifty-sixth year, at Ostia.",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005#CCELNPNF101v.14",
    "work_id": "ccel-npnf1/npnf101/005",
    "canonical_ref": "CCELNPNF101v.14",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "388. Aug. revisits Rome, and then returns to Africa. Adeodatus, full of promise, dies.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": null,
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "post_schism": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
